e381dd26-329b-42d0-97bd-d6d3d3d5e6b8	66b0d5f8-b0aa-4bbb-842c-9bb4c3f25b29	I just received the prints I’ll be bringing to next Sunday’s meetup in Rotterdam (a week from tomorrow), and I’m really looking forward to sharing them and seeing everyone else’s work.\n\nCurious to hear your thoughts, exchange ideas, and maybe, if there’s interest, head out for a short shoot together afterwards. I’ll bring my camera as well.	2026-04-18 10:43:15.017512+00	2026-04-18 10:43:15.017512+00	\N	\N	\N
159c420f-acec-4c01-b080-56e11abf6bdf	36ae98cf-e596-4157-8eb7-4391c5292b7f	Hi Gerard! That sounds great!\nI'm curious about your prints and if weather permits we can definitely go out for some photos. See you then!	2026-04-18 10:54:33.72656+00	2026-04-18 10:54:33.72656+00	\N	e381dd26-329b-42d0-97bd-d6d3d3d5e6b8	\N
3cead9ac-3738-496d-936c-ab5cbd8f351b	36ae98cf-e596-4157-8eb7-4391c5292b7f	Hey everyone, the forecast is showing some non-ideal weather for sunset light. It might be gray and cloudy. There's also a storm coming, but only around 22:00 (after the walk).\n\nJust a heads-up, we are still proceeding with the walk! See you in a bit 🤗	2026-05-02 13:07:27.525511+00	2026-05-02 13:07:27.525511+00	\N	\N	\N
74704c45-82dc-45d3-a352-21bfeb4d1953	36ae98cf-e596-4157-8eb7-4391c5292b7f	Hey everyone! I see there is a huge interest in the photo walk coming Saturday at Kralingse Plas, that's great!\n\nAs mentioned, we're planning on having lunch first. Since we're with a large crowd, I wanted to make a reservation at the restaurant.\n\nYou're not required to have lunch with us, as you can skip this and arrive an hour later (13:00) and just join for the walk - it's up to you!\n\nFor the people who want to have lunch, I'd like to know the count so I can make the reservation. The menu can be found here: https://www.restaurantdetuin.nl/eten-en-drinken/reserveren-tot-10-personen/lunch-keuzemenus\n\nPlease let me know if you're having lunch with us! Thank you!	2026-07-13 14:01:35.277221+00	2026-07-13 14:33:49.575575+00	\N	\N	2026-07-13 14:34:05.298+00
d776049b-6688-41d2-83e1-6aa390d50d7c	36ae98cf-e596-4157-8eb7-4391c5292b7f	Wow, love these. I kinda do like the colors, even tho they're more warm/red/magenta tinted.\nCan you please add the camera, lens, other info in the description? 😁	2026-01-16 13:44:21.411196+00	2026-01-16 13:44:21.411196+00	\N	\N	\N
9d31702a-0fef-4cd2-a812-09e28290eac4	36ae98cf-e596-4157-8eb7-4391c5292b7f	Hey y'all, a little update with gear info for shooting directly into the sun. In short:\n1. Lens: 300mm+\n2. Filter: ND100000 filter\n3. Tripod, extra batteries\n4. Whatever you need to be comfortable for being 2 hours outside in the evening. See you next week!\n\nRequired gear:\n1. Lens\nIf you want to shoot the eclipse head-on, the subject will be tiny. A large zoom lens would be optimal. Anything below 300mm will be quite small. Of course if you want to take other types of photos, having a lens with a large aperture will help with the low light conditions of the eclipse.\n\n2. Filter\nAny certified solar eclipse filter will do. Officially you'll need a ND100000 filter to shoot into direct sunlight - otherwise you might risk destroying your camera's sensor. Note: I will bring an A4 of solar filter film with some tape and scissors. We can make some DIY filters with that, but use at your own risk!\n\n3. Tripod\nAny sturdy tripod that you don't mind getting sandy will do. We will be standing there for about 2 hours, so not having to hold it and aligning for the perfect shot is nice!\n\n4. Extra batteries, jacket, water & snacks\nWe'll be outside for a while, come prepared!	2026-08-06 20:57:58.559039+00	2026-08-06 20:57:58.559039+00	\N	\N	\N
98049e86-b6db-481f-a0db-fa772e3f5ae4	36ae98cf-e596-4157-8eb7-4391c5292b7f	Hey y'all\nasdasd	2026-09-04 17:32:24.747452+00	2026-09-04 17:32:29.164555+00	2026-09-04 17:33:04.577+00	\N	\N
7db7f75b-4b31-4265-9c35-d339eff6e37c	bb1f198b-0f2a-452c-875b-23b8b949af4e	Cute ❤️	2026-01-31 12:44:03.125472+00	2026-01-31 12:44:03.125472+00	\N	\N	\N
ee5f658c-9502-4497-9e66-2eb743a98ea1	bb1f198b-0f2a-452c-875b-23b8b949af4e	Get closer	2026-01-31 12:45:03.571962+00	2026-01-31 12:45:03.571962+00	\N	\N	\N
